WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:03.929
Have you ever seen this statue in New York City?

2
00:00:03.930 --> 00:00:07.760
It's a statue of a sled dog named Balto.

3
00:00:07.761 --> 00:00:12.418
He's famous for running in Alaska's "Great Race of Mercy."

4
00:00:12.419 --> 00:00:15.529
Balto was a Siberian husky.

5
00:00:15.530 --> 00:00:19.620
He worked as a sled dog, carrying supplies to miners.

6
00:00:19.621 --> 00:00:27.830
Then, in January 1925, a disease called diphtheria broke out in the city of Nome, Alaska.

7
00:00:27.831 --> 00:00:32.518
Children were in danger, and the disease was spreading fast.

8
00:00:32.519 --> 00:00:37.154
Doctors needed medicine, but there was no way to get it to Nome.

9
00:00:37.155 --> 00:00:43.639
Weather conditions were terrible, so planes couldn't fly, and the sea was full of ice.

10
00:00:43.640 --> 00:00:50.569
The nearest train station was 1,085 kilometers away in Nenana.

11
00:00:50.570 --> 00:00:56.599
There was only one solution for this frozen land—dogsleds!

12
00:00:56.600 --> 00:01:00.466
The medicine would be sent to Nenana by train.

13
00:01:00.467 --> 00:01:07.255
Then twenty mushers would transport the medicine by dogsled in a relay race to Nome.

14
00:01:07.256 --> 00:01:12.825
Balto's owner, Leonhard Seppala, didn't think Balto was special.

15
00:01:12.826 --> 00:01:18.895
So he chose a dog named Togo to lead his sled, and didn't put Balto on his team.

16
00:01:18.896 --> 00:01:23.937
But a musher named Gunnar Kaasen knew Balto well.

17
00:01:23.938 --> 00:01:27.678
He thought Balto was smart and strong.

18
00:01:27.679 --> 00:01:30.962
He made Balto the leader of his team.

19
00:01:30.963 --> 00:01:36.725
On January 27 the first musher picked up the medicine in Nenana.

20
00:01:36.726 --> 00:01:42.739
It was packed in a metal cylinder, and the whole package weighed nine kilograms.

21
00:01:42.740 --> 00:01:50.558
When the musher's sled set out, it was dark and freezing cold—45 degrees below zero!

22
00:01:50.559 --> 00:01:55.841
But his team ran well, delivering the medicine to the next team.

23
00:01:55.842 --> 00:01:58.674
On and on the relay went.

24
00:01:58.675 --> 00:02:02.951
Some dogs died when their lungs burst from the cold.

25
00:02:02.952 --> 00:02:07.313
While Balto and Kaasen waited, the weather grew worse.

26
00:02:07.314 --> 00:02:13.197
Then, five days after the race began, Balto heard barking.

27
00:02:13.198 --> 00:02:15.239
The sled was here!

28
00:02:15.240 --> 00:02:19.565
When Balto took off, fierce winds howled.

29
00:02:19.566 --> 00:02:23.575
Snow swirled, blinding Kaasen.

30
00:02:23.576 --> 00:02:27.001
Most people thought Balto would lose track of the trail.

31
00:02:27.002 --> 00:02:30.042
Yet Balto kept running well.

32
00:02:30.059 --> 00:02:34.321
Suddenly a powerful wind gust blew the dogs off the trail.

33
00:02:34.322 --> 00:02:37.430
The medicine flew off the sled!

34
00:02:37.431 --> 00:02:41.083
Kaasen frantically searched for it in the snow.

35
00:02:41.084 --> 00:02:48.003
By the time he found the package, his hands were frozen.

36
00:02:48.004 --> 00:02:50.681
Then the team took off again!

37
00:02:50.682 --> 00:02:53.672
Finally the team reached its stop.

38
00:02:53.673 --> 00:02:58.021
But the building where the next musher was waiting looked dark.

39
00:02:58.022 --> 00:03:01.153
Kaasen thought the musher was asleep.

40
00:03:01.154 --> 00:03:05.134
To save time he decided to keep going.

41
00:03:05.135 --> 00:03:13.209
On February 2, after running for seven and a half hours, Balto's team reached Nome.

42
00:03:13.210 --> 00:03:19.073
Balto had led them for 85 kilometers, through darkness and a blizzard.

43
00:03:19.074 --> 00:03:24.897
They had safely delivered the medicine, saving the town from disaster.

44
00:03:24.898 --> 00:03:29.308
News of Balto and Kaasen's heroic run spread quickly.

45
00:03:29.309 --> 00:03:35.616
The heroes appeared in newspapers, and Balto's statue was placed here in Central Park.

46
00:03:35.617 --> 00:03:40.194
The two even starred in a silent movie about the race.

47
00:03:40.195 --> 00:03:46.797
Balto's owner, however, felt ignored and jealous of Balto and Kaasen's fame.

48
00:03:46.798 --> 00:03:51.293
Eventually, Balto was sold to a traveling show.

49
00:03:51.294 --> 00:03:57.615
After that, he was sold again to another show where he lived in terrible conditions.

50
00:03:57.616 --> 00:04:06.295
Luckily, some people rescued him and found him a new home at a zoo in Cleveland, Ohio.

51
00:04:06.296 --> 00:04:11.099
Today Balto is still famous for delivering the medicine to Nome.

52
00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:18.838
I like to visit his statue and read these words: "Endurance, Fidelity, Intelligence."

53
00:04:18.839 --> 00:04:24.187
What a hero!

